$$

This simplifies to:

$$
45 \times 40320 \times \sum_{k=0}^{8} 10^k
$$

The sum of powers of 10 from $10^0$ to $10^8$ is a **geometric series**:

$$
\sum_{k=0}^{8} 10^k = \frac{10^9 - 1}{10 - 1} = \frac{1000000000 - 1}{9} = \frac{999999999}{9} = 111111111
$$

So now we can plug this into the formula:

$$
\text{Total Sum} = 45 \times 40320 \times 111111111
$$

---

